<Doc lang={lang} page="blocks" current="Post" title="Post"
  description="Post in FLOAT: the layer-based finishing page and the Output block that ends every workflow. Layers, masks, blend modes, filters, simplified sliders, versions and export, with the published sources.">

  <p class="kicker">Block</p>
  <h1>Post</h1>
  <p class="meta">FLOAT 0.2.0 · beta of {release.date.en}</p>

  <dl class="inshort"><div><dt>What it does</dt><dd>It is where the picture is finished: each workflow’s result is a layer, and every adjustment is a filter that can be changed or removed at any time.</dd></div><div><dt>What it shows</dt><dd>The final picture, the layers panel beside it, and a few sliders from 0 to 4 that start in the middle.</dd></div><div><dt>What can be set</dt><dd>Sky, Contrast and Saturation first; the default rendering is a sound starting point, and Export writes the final file, a 16-bit TIFF by default.</dd></div></dl>

  <aside class="note toc">
    <b>On this page</b>
